      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.01",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "Starting Strength is a unit's initial model count. Half-strength and Below Half-strength are determined from that count, or from remaining wounds for a single-model unit.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-01-starting-strength-and-half-strength"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "8dc3caba94393fa0b470536b29c2596234cc8f538b7066bbe5f62ac26884db28",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.02",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "An effect with a stated duration continues for that full duration, including through embarkation or Strategic Reserves. If no duration is stated, it lasts only for the specified period or the phase in which it was given.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-02-persisting-rules-effects"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "7f52da86cb0b17f560b05cb4647cce5c2cb5ab79037e57b3b325aeb3687a3209",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.03",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "Revived, returned or added models cannot take a unit above Starting Strength and must follow the applicable placement, wargear, wounds and Transport restrictions. A revived Leader or Support model returns as a separate unit.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-03-revived-and-adding-models-to-a-unit"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "7123a09e7be4c2c61399ca58079e6d1d4e95ba0198ef18ccfdc6e879f8424a41",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.04",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "Embarked units and units in Strategic Reserves are not on the battlefield, so visibility and distance normally cannot be measured to or from them.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-04-not-on-the-battlefield"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "e55c7b8e472aeb609155ee1edd7e110790e9c695a8957c9fb739beb14598e736",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.05",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "?Other? means a different model or unit from the one already identified, including another instance of the same datasheet.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-05-other-model-unit"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "fd7f32138d122f4e9dc5bcf1d5f4b2fb19c7369c5171338161c786d85bdecc35",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.06",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "A unit split before battle becomes separate smaller units, and each resulting unit uses its own model count as its Starting Strength.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-06-splitting-units"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "09920dbfc339dca6068f9e63b64c3bada70ded09df47499721c5262639bb0a7f",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.07",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "A descriptor applies to a unit if at least one model in that unit meets it; it does not automatically give that descriptor to every model.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-07-describing-units"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "5fbddcdadac36fe38f11a733729d1ca436124af49430117815e597ba0c9bc704",
      "editorialRevision": "editorial-review-2026-09-14",
      "field": "summary",
      "semanticSource": {
        "documentId": "core-rules",
        "locator": "01.02.08",
        "revision": "11e"
      },
      "summary": "When a rule says ?a? unit, model or object without an exact number, it means one or more rather than exactly one.",
      "termId": "core-rule-01-02-08-a-unit-model-object"
    },
    {
      "contentHash": "a2872bc8a18154af4f77b8e1be11e0256f59a3f91531d99cdad620cad98ea49f",
